# CODEOWNERS — who gets auto-requested as a reviewer for each area.
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Format: <pattern>  <owner> [<owner> ...]
# Match precedence: LAST matching line wins. Catch-all goes first.

# Default owner — every path, unless overridden below.
*                               @Orange-The-World

# Adapters — new connectors expand the trust surface. Require an owner review.
/server/adapters/               @Orange-The-World

# Server + auth + sync logic.
/server/                        @Orange-The-World

# Supabase schema + RLS — migrations are the source of truth.
/supabase/                      @Orange-The-World

# Cryptographic primitives (vault key derivation, ciphertext shape, link widget).
/src/lib/                       @Orange-The-World

# Docs — narrative surface of the project.
/README.md                      @Orange-The-World
/CONTRIBUTING.md                @Orange-The-World
/SECURITY.md                    @Orange-The-World
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md             @Orange-The-World
/docs/                          @Orange-The-World

# GitHub workflows + community health files.
/.github/                       @Orange-The-World

# Workflow definitions. A change here can change what CI is allowed to do, so
# the reviewing account signs it specifically. This line must stay BELOW the
# /.github/ entry above: CODEOWNERS resolves by LAST match, so putting it first
# would make it inert.
/.github/workflows/             @Making-the-World-Orange
